{"id": "e8699511-1638-4819-8f9b-e1119df4b991", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T15:37:04.743015", "source": "user", "parent_id": "c5f90b72-30e1-469b-a274-27173ebe8615", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Hello. This is a design-only task: produce a final experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) for the question, 'Will chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting improve the task-solving ability of LLM-based agents in WorkArena++?'. Execution and benchmarks are not required and the runtime is offline (no network, no preinstalled dependencies, no GPU), so treat this strictly as a methodological design deliverable grounded in known public facts about WorkArena++ and CoT prompting research — do not fabricate measured results, exact numbers from prior papers, or specific task IDs that you have not verified from the supplied documents/workspace. Keep the final write-up self-contained and rigorous so it could in principle be executed later by someone else with the right compute and API access. For this first turn, please do the following and nothing more — no full design yet. The deliverable I want from this round is exactly the three items below, in a single reply, with no long preamble: 1) INPUT / REPOSITORY INSPECTION (≤1 short paragraph + a compact list): inspect /workspace and any documents or topics I supplied (note: track.md only states this is design-only). Report (a) what you found in the repo (files, configs, scripts, anything LLM/eval-related) and (b) any constraints or signals you can extract from the supplied documents or researcher_topics. If nothing relevant exists, say so explicitly. Do not run heavy installs or network calls. 2) PROPOSED APPROACH (terse, skimmable): outline the design you would carry out, including — research question restated as an operational hypothesis with a primary endpoint and at least one secondary endpoint; conditions/cells (e.g., No-CoT vs. CoT, and any auxiliary factors such as CoT style: zero-shot 'Let's think step by step' vs. few-shot worked examples vs. self-consistency, vs. tool-augmented variants); platform (WorkArena++, what it is, what tasks/Browsergym version you'd assume, what tier of tasks — list, plan, search, forms, config — you'd cover, and how you'd split them, e.g., by difficulty or category); agent stack (underlying LLM, browser driver, observation/action format, prompt template structure, where CoT is inserted — before action, before long-horizon subgoals, or after observation — and how you control for length/dollar cost); protocol (per-task trials, retry policy, max steps, timeouts, seeding, environment state reset, randomization/stratification); controls and confounders (model identity, prompt-length budget, exemplar shuffling, temperature, tool access, caching, antitampering / parameter leakage from CoT, order effects); metrics beyond success rate (step efficiency, tokens/cost, latency, number of reasoning errors, hallucination/loop rate, failure-mode taxonomy, calibration if feasible); and analysis plan (statistical test paired by task, correction for multiple comparisons, effect size + CIs, stratified breakdown by task category/difficulty, ablations). 3) ASSUMPTIONS & UNCERTAINTIES (bulleted): list every consequential assumption you are making because the brief is underspecified — e.g., baseline agent and LLM to assume, WorkArena++ version and inclusion rules, definition of 'improve' (success rate vs. cost-adjusted score), what counts as a fair CoT implementation, sample-size philosophy given no execution, whether results generalize across task families, threats to construct validity (CoT leakage into non-CoT condition via instructions), threats to external validity (a single model, a single prompt template), and anything else you think materially affects the design. Flag the top 1–2 items you would most want me to confirm before you proceed to the full design. Stop after these three items; do not produce the full design, abstract, or results yet.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Will the chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting mechanism improve the task-solving ability of LLM-based agents in WorkArena++?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
