{"id": "08aa0661-d11d-4bdf-952e-3b3edb2b9e8a", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T15:38:01.624754", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "5d4e5980-4d2d-4114-b938-8af11a5fdcf2", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-162ec459-cbaf-4518-8341-c3017b09a130", "tool_call": {"id": "call-162ec459-cbaf-4518-8341-c3017b09a130", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Initial plan: repo inspection, approach, assumptions\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## 1) INPUT / REPOSITORY INSPECTION\\n\\nThe `/workspace` directory contains a single file, `task.json`. No code, configs, scripts, datasets, or external documents are present; the in-file `track.md` field simply states \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" The `researcher_topics` entry (\\\"neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1\\\") has no retrievable document content in this environment (no `track.md`/PDFs on disk, no network, no installed packages — `python3`, `workarena*`, `browsergym` are not present). In short: there is nothing in the repository that constrains the design, so every concrete setup choice below is an assumption the researcher must ratify rather than an observation from supplied material.\\n\\nCompact list of what is actually present:\\n- `/workspace/task.json` — only artifact; contains the question, a `design-only` context note, and a `track.md` field that is a one-line placeholder (not a fetched document).\\n- No `*.py`, `*.yaml`, `*.json` configs, no benchmark tasks, no agent/eval scripts, no environment manifests, no model prompts.\\n- No installed dependencies; no GPU; no network. Confirmed `python3` is not on PATH and no WorkArena/BrowserGym packages are importable.\\n\\n## 2) PROPOSED APPROACH (terse)\\n\\n**Hypothesis (operational).** Primary: adding explicit chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning to an LLM agent's per-step prompt on WorkArena++ increases mean task success rate at fixed task-set, fixed model, and fixed observation/action interface. Primary endpoint = mean success-rate Δ (CoT − No-CoT), paired by task. Secondary endpoints: (a) cost-adjusted score = success per 1k total tokens, (b) median steps-to-success, (c) reasoning-error/hallucination/loop rate from a failure-mode taxonomy, (d) calibration (Brier score on the agent's own \\\"I am done\\\" confidence, optional), and (e) effect-size heterogeneity across task tiers.\\n\\n**Conditions (cells).** Factor 1: *Reasoning style* — within-subject across every task:\\n- C0 No-CoT: direct action emission (control).\\n- C1 Zero-shot CoT: \\\"Let's think step by step\\\" before action.\\n- C2 Few-shot CoT: k=3–5 worked (thinking, action, observation) exemplars drawn from the same tier.\\n- C3 Self-consistency: C1 sampled at temperature 0.7 × N=5, majority-vote on the emitted action.\\n- (Optional) C4 Tool-augmented CoT: explicit \\\"scratchpad\\\" sub-tool (e.g., `plan`, `verify`) inserted between thought and action; same prompt budget as C1.\\nFactor 2 (blocking): *WorkArena++ tier* (only those tiers the researcher confirms exist; my list below is provisional and unverified): list/lookup, search/navigation, forms, configuration, and any \\\"plan\\\" tier. Tasks are blocked (stratified) by tier to support within-tier paired analysis.\\n\\n**Platform.** WorkArena++ (ServiceNow atomic + composite tasks, served via BrowserGym). Assume one ServiceNow instance per worker with deterministic reset between trials. Task selection: all tasks of each selected tier run; otherwise a stratified random sample of N tasks per tier with tier share proportional to population. Because the exact tier names and task IDs are NOT verified from the workspace, the design treats the tier list as a parameter to be filled in by the researcher.\\n\\n**Agent stack.**\\n- Base LLM: a single frontier chat model (the researcher's choice; default proposed = a current mid-size model such as GPT-4-class / Claude-3-class with deterministic decoding, temperature 0 for C0/C1/C2, 0.7 for C3, top-p 1, seed fixed). Same model identity across all conditions.\\n- Browser driver: BrowserGym over a headless Chromium controlling a ServiceNow instance.\\n- Observation → prompt: HTML-ax-tree (or DOM-pruned) snippet + last action + last error + current goal string + chat history of (thought, action, observation) tuples. Action format = BrowserGym's discrete action space enum.\\n- Where CoT is inserted: immediately before the action token, in a dedicated `<think>...</think>` channel that is also logged and later used for failure coding. Length-controlled by an instruction \\\"Use ≤ N tokens of reasoning where N≈120\\\"; cost-budget matched across conditions where possible.\\n- Prompt template: one shared system prompt; only the reasoning-instruction block differs between C0 vs. C1/C2/C3.\\n\\n**Protocol.**\\n- Trials: 3 independent trials per (task × condition) to absorb stochasticity; median used for paired tests.\\n- Max steps: 25 per task (or tier-specific cap); wall-clock timeout 10 min/trial.\\n- Retry policy: no retries inside a trial; a trial that errors out for infrastructural reasons is rerun at most once and flagged.\\n- Seeding: Python/NumPy seeds, BrowserGym instance snapshot ID, ServiceNow user fixed.\\n- State reset: hard rollback to a known post-login ServiceNow state before every trial; verified by a sentinel page load.\\n- Randomization: Latin-square ordering of conditions across tasks; exemplars in C2 shuffled per trial from a fixed pool of k.\\n\\n**Controls & confounders.**\\n- Prompt-length and token cost: C0 receives a filler \\\"state your plan in 1 short sentence then act\\\" instruction of comparable verbosity so that prompt length is not a free parameter.\\n- Exemplar shuffle and exemplar-pool identity held fixed.\\n- Identical temperature across deterministic conditions (C0/C1/C2).\\n- Tool access identical (same BrowserGym action set; no extra retrievers).\\n- Caching disabled for the agent's HTTP calls; enabled for static prompt scaffolding to control cost.\\n- Antitampering checks: a held-out \\\"canary\\\" task variant where the No-CoT prompt is patched to include the literal CoT phrase — must NOT change its behaviour, validating that gains in C1–C3 are not instruction artefacts leaking.\\n- Order effects: counterbalanced with Latin square; treatment of \\\"first-trial contamination\\\" analysed as a covariate.\\n\\n**Metrics beyond success rate.**\\n- Step efficiency: steps / optimal-steps (where an upper bound is known from WorkArena++ task definitions).\\n- Tokens: input + output per trial; success per 1k tokens; $ per success.\\n- Latency: wall-clock seconds per trial and per step.\\n- Reasoning-error taxonomy (manual coding of failed trials): (i) wrong goal interpretation, (ii) hallucinated UI element, (iii) action-format/parse error, (iv) loop/repeat of an identical (state, action), (v) premature stop, (vi) incorrect post-condition check.\\n- Calibration: Brier score on self-reported \\\"done\\\" confidence (only if the prompt asks for it; same instruction in all conditions).\\n\\n**Analysis plan.**\\n- Primary test: paired (task-level) two-sided test of success between C1 and C0 (and separately C2 vs. C0, C3 vs. C0); subject-level pairing because every task sees every condition.\\n- Correction: Holm–Bonferroni across the 3 primary CoT contrasts.\\n- Effect sizes: Cohen's d for paired proportions + bootstrap 95% CI on Δ; same for cost-adjusted score.\\n- Stratified breakdown: by tier (interaction test); pre-registered \\\"where does CoT help / hurt\\\" decomposition.\\n- Ablations: drop scratchpad (C1 vs C4); few-shot count k ∈ {1,3,5}; prompt-length matched sub-analysis removing CoT text and re-inserting equivalent filler.\\n- Robustness: rerun top 10% of tasks from each tier with seed variation to estimate variance.\\n- All analyses are *registered in advance of execution* against this design.\\n\\n**Feasibility check.** No execution is attempted here. Risks to feasibility when run: API cost (mitigated by ≤ N tasks/tier and by 3 trials; estimate dominated by the C3 self-consistency arm at 5× the C1 token bill), BrowserGym instance provisioning (requires a ServiceNow PDIs or shared testing tenant), and evaluation wall-clock (mitigated by parallelisation across CPUs).\\n\\n## 3) ASSUMPTIONS & UNCERTAINTIES\\n\\n- WorkArena++ is assumed to be the ServiceNow benchmark suite built on BrowserGym, with tiers spanning list/lookup, search/navigation, forms, and configuration-style tasks; the exact tier names and counts are NOT verified from the supplied materials.\\n- \\\"Improve\\\" is treated as a paired Δ in success rate (primary) plus a cost-adjusted secondary endpoint; pure-success and cost-adjusted metrics can disagree, so the design reports both.\\n- No-CoT baseline is assumed to be a direct-action prompt with matched verbosity; CoT is assumed to be inserted as a <think>…</think> step immediately before action emission (not after observation only, not at subgoal granularity only).\\n- CoT variants are restricted to Zero-shot, Few-shot, and Self-consistency; a tool-augmented scratchpad variant is optional and treated as an ablation, not a primary contrast.\\n- A single base model is used across all conditions to isolate the effect of CoT; cross-model generality is acknowledged as a threat to external validity rather than measured.\\n- Trials-per-cell = 3; this is a design choice for budgetary reasons — power analyses are deferred to the full design and should be re-checked with the researcher.\\n- No published WorkArena++ success-rate numbers, task IDs, or paper-specific statistics are cited because they are not verifiable from the supplied workspace and must not be fabricated.\\n- Construct-validity threats: (a) CoT \\\"leaking\\\" into the No-CoT condition via matched-verbosity filler, controlled by a canary task; (b) exemplar contamination where C2 exemplars overlap with test tasks, controlled by disjoint splits.\\n- External-validity threats: single model, single prompt template, single BrowserGym/ServiceNow version, English-only UI.\\n- Statistical assumptions: paired task-level analysis assumes tasks are exchangeable units; we therefore also report tier-stratified effects rather than only a pooled Δ.\\n\\n**Top items I would like you to confirm before I produce the full design:**\\n1. Primary endpoint definition — *does \\\"improve\\\" mean success-rate gain, cost-adjusted gain, or \\\"must improve on both\\\"?* This single choice can flip the conclusion and dictates the analysis hierarchy.\\n2. Scope of CoT conditions — *is the contrast set C0/C1/C2/C3 acceptable, or do you want only one CoT variant (e.g., Zero-shot only) as the headline comparison, with the others as ablations?*\\n\\n(Secondary, also worth a sentence: which base model and which WorkArena++ tier list to use as the default.)\",\"evidence\":\"Repository inspection: `ls -la /workspace` returns only `task.json` (415 bytes). `find / -maxdepth 3 -type f` confirms no other project files. `cat /workspace/task.json` shows the question, a `context` field flagging \\\"Design-only\\\", and a `documents.track.md` field whose value is the string \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" (i.e., not a fetched document). System scan (`find / -name track.md`, `find / -path '*neurips*' -name '*.md'`) returns no results. `which python3` is unavailable and `pip3 list` shows no WorkArena/BrowserGym packages; `task.json` also states `network: disabled`, `gpu_enabled: false`, `software_environment: \\\"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\\\"`. Thus no concrete WorkArena++ version, task ID, tier name, model identifier, or numeric baseline from prior work is source-grounded in the workspace and any such details in the full design must be treated as researcher-ratified assumptions rather than observed facts.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\