nged in difficulty — this is a design choice to confirm.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Whether WorkArena++ tasks permit multiple valid solutions (which would change the success criterion and the calibration analysis).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether failure-mode coding is performed manually, by a judge LLM, or both; affects metric validity.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether the agent stack should mirror a specific published setup (e.g., BrowserGym's default RLM-style loop) or be designed from scratch; affects reproducibility.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"CoT condition set — whether to compare only Zero-shot CoT to No-CoT (headline), or to include Few-shot and Self-consistency as first-class cells.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Definition of \\\"improve\\\" — success-rate Δ vs. cost-adjusted score vs. requiring both. Single most consequential choice.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Which LLM serves as the base model — affects absolute performance and the headroom for CoT to help.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Exact WorkArena++ tier taxonomy and task-pool sizes — must be confirmed before the full design can fix sample-size allocation per stratum.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-95b94049-5e0f-4765-869d-d470f353716e", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
