ity.\n- U7 Whether WorkArena++ tasks permit multiple valid solutions (would change the success criterion and the calibration analysis).\n- U8 Construct-validity check: a canary task that injects CoT phrasing into the No-CoT prompt must remain unchanged in difficulty — design choice to confirm.\n\nTop items I would like you to confirm before I produce the full design:\n1. Primary endpoint definition — does \"improve\" mean success-rate gain, cost-adjusted gain, or \"must improve on both\"? This single choice can flip the conclusion and dictates the analysis hierarchy.\n2. Scope of CoT conditions — is the contrast set C0/C1/C2/C3 acceptable, or do you want only one CoT variant (e.g., Zero-shot only) as the headline comparison, with the others as ablations?\n\n(Secondary, also worth a sentence: which base model and which WorkArena++ tier list to use as the default.)", "evidence": "Repository inspection: `ls -la /workspace` returned only `task.json` (415 bytes). `find / -maxdepth 3 -type f` confirmed no other project files exist. `cat /workspace/task.json` showed the public question, a `context` field flagging \"Design-only\", and a `documents.track.md` field whose value is the string \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" (i.e., not a fetched document). System scan (`find / -name track.md`, `find / -path '*neurips*' -name '*.md'`) returned no results. `which python3` was unavailable and `pip3 list` showed no WorkArena/BrowserGym packages; `task.json` further states `network: disabled`, `gpu_enabled: false`, `software_environment: \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\"`. No concrete WorkArena++ version, tier name, task ID, model identifier, or numeric baseline from prior work is source-grounded in the workspace, so any such detail in the full design must be treated as a researcher-ratified assumption rather than an observed fact.", "assumptions": ["A1 WorkArena++ is interpreted as the BrowserGym/ServiceNow benchmark with broad